WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.102 --> 00:00:01.320
- Good morning, Believe Nation.

00:00:01.320 --> 00:00:04.570
Today's message is overcome your fears.

00:00:05.559 --> 00:00:07.976
Over to you Gabrielle Bernstein.

00:00:07.976 --> 00:00:09.726
(rooster crows)

00:00:09.726 --> 00:00:12.507
♫ I wake up every morning

00:00:12.507 --> 00:00:15.447
♫ Espresso keep me going

00:00:15.447 --> 00:00:19.461
♫ I wake up every morning

00:00:19.461 --> 00:00:21.208
- What's the first step
to overcoming the fear

00:00:21.208 --> 00:00:23.331
or transforming the fear?

00:00:23.331 --> 00:00:24.632
- To witness it.

00:00:24.632 --> 00:00:27.576
To be the non-judgemental witness of it.

00:00:27.576 --> 00:00:30.885
To look at it and say,
something's got to give.

00:00:30.885 --> 00:00:35.052
So, if you're unwilling to
look at your fear head on

00:00:36.601 --> 00:00:40.022
and honor it and witness,
I would say if you don't

00:00:40.022 --> 00:00:42.775
show up for what's up, it
would it will keep showing up.

00:00:42.775 --> 00:00:45.008
So looking at saying,
I witness my resistance

00:00:45.008 --> 00:00:47.409
and you see that fear as resistance,

00:00:47.409 --> 00:00:51.390
fear is the resistance to
what it is that you desire.

00:00:51.390 --> 00:00:53.877
And in the absence of
resistance, you become a magnet

00:00:53.877 --> 00:00:56.739
for what you desire, when
you let go of that fear

00:00:56.739 --> 00:00:58.989
and you transcend that
fear, that's when you start

00:00:58.989 --> 00:01:01.172
to become a super attractor.

00:01:01.172 --> 00:01:04.649
That's when you start to let what is truly

00:01:04.649 --> 00:01:07.914
of essence for you in your
life, what is truly of service

00:01:07.914 --> 00:01:09.555
for you into your life,
what is true happiness

00:01:09.555 --> 00:01:12.593
into your life and so looking at the fear,

00:01:12.593 --> 00:01:14.363
witnessing it, calling it by its name,

00:01:14.363 --> 00:01:16.817
and even if you don't have the tools yet,

00:01:16.817 --> 00:01:18.474
what happens is when you look at the fear

00:01:18.474 --> 00:01:21.341
and you're like oh, I see this
fear, I see this resistance,

00:01:21.341 --> 00:01:23.449
I see how it's blocking
my life and I choose

00:01:23.449 --> 00:01:24.737
to see it differently.

00:01:24.737 --> 00:01:26.935
That's when you're listening
to an audio like this.

00:01:26.935 --> 00:01:28.975
That's when a book like
yours will fall off a shelf.

00:01:28.975 --> 00:01:29.808
- [Lewis] The catalyst.

00:01:29.808 --> 00:01:32.480
- Yeah, exactly, you open up
your consciousness pretty much.

00:01:32.480 --> 00:01:34.443
You crack open your
consciousness to find solutions

00:01:34.443 --> 00:01:35.947
rather than fight problems.

00:01:35.947 --> 00:01:37.520
So when you're not looking at the fear,

00:01:37.520 --> 00:01:38.721
you're just living in the fear

00:01:38.721 --> 00:01:39.958
and you're believing in the problem.

00:01:39.958 --> 00:01:40.950
But when you witness the fear

00:01:40.950 --> 00:01:42.191
and you're willing to see it differently,

00:01:42.191 --> 00:01:43.539
you start living in the solution.

00:01:43.539 --> 00:01:45.737
- I think the key to overcoming your fear

00:01:45.737 --> 00:01:47.295
is the awareness of the fear.

00:01:47.295 --> 00:01:49.460
I think most people aren't even aware

00:01:49.460 --> 00:01:51.304
of their biggest fears
that are holding them back

00:01:51.304 --> 00:01:54.962
on a daily basis in their
business and in their lives.

00:01:54.962 --> 00:01:57.540
What often happens is somebody
gives you an opportunity.

00:01:57.540 --> 00:01:59.915
Come speak at this event
or here's this project

00:01:59.915 --> 00:02:01.911
to work with this person
or go on this date,

00:02:01.911 --> 00:02:03.833
whatever it is, you get an opportunity,

00:02:03.833 --> 00:02:05.492
and the real fear you have is

00:02:05.492 --> 00:02:06.950
that you're not good enough.

00:02:06.950 --> 00:02:08.289
That you're going to fail.

00:02:08.289 --> 00:02:10.032
That you're not going
to give a good result.

00:02:10.032 --> 00:02:12.004
That's really the fear deep down inside

00:02:12.004 --> 00:02:15.609
when you come up with, I
don't have the time to do it.

00:02:15.609 --> 00:02:17.721
I don't have the time to do
it is the biggest BS excuse

00:02:17.721 --> 00:02:18.908
of all time.

00:02:18.908 --> 00:02:21.787
You may not be making the
priority to go out and do it

00:02:21.787 --> 00:02:23.749
but we all have the same amount of time.

00:02:23.749 --> 00:02:27.319
You should never say
I don't have the time.

00:02:27.319 --> 00:02:29.107
You can say I choose not to do it.

00:02:29.107 --> 00:02:30.802
I choose not to make the time.

00:02:30.802 --> 00:02:32.292
But as soon you say I don't have the time,

00:02:32.292 --> 00:02:34.274
you abdicate responsibility.

00:02:34.274 --> 00:02:35.684
You are in control.

00:02:35.684 --> 00:02:38.180
You get to pick what you do
with your 24 hours everyday.

00:02:38.180 --> 00:02:41.662
It's the one thing that is
equal across every human being.

00:02:41.662 --> 00:02:43.269
We all have 24 hours.

00:02:43.269 --> 00:02:46.429
So we disguise our real fear
with some practical reason.

00:02:46.429 --> 00:02:48.786
We say we don't have the time,
we don't have the resources,

00:02:48.786 --> 00:02:50.005
blah blah blah, whatever it is

00:02:50.005 --> 00:02:52.129
but really it's some kind of fear.

00:02:52.129 --> 00:02:54.730
And I think that's the
case for a lot of people.

00:02:54.730 --> 00:02:56.269
So many of our fears are so subconscious

00:02:56.269 --> 00:02:59.320
and we're so, we do it so automatically,

00:02:59.320 --> 00:03:01.691
every single day and
we've convinced ourselves

00:03:01.691 --> 00:03:03.421
there's a logical reason behind it.

00:03:03.421 --> 00:03:05.957
So the first step in my mind
is the awareness of the fear.

00:03:05.957 --> 00:03:08.094
The awareness that it's
not a lack of resources.

00:03:08.094 --> 00:03:10.484
The awareness is not a lack of time.

00:03:10.484 --> 00:03:11.966
And it's really that, I'm just afraid

00:03:11.966 --> 00:03:14.953
that I'm going to fail and I
don't want to do it anymore.

00:03:14.953 --> 00:03:17.573
So awareness of the
fear is the first thing.

00:03:17.573 --> 00:03:19.574
Next thing is, do you have
to why to get out of it.

00:03:19.574 --> 00:03:21.340
Is it important to break that thing?

00:03:21.340 --> 00:03:23.581
Is it important to
crush through that fear?

00:03:23.581 --> 00:03:27.247
Do you have a strong enough
reason to make a painful change?

00:03:27.247 --> 00:03:30.611
And when you do, the third
step is to start to catch it.

00:03:30.611 --> 00:03:32.231
And you often can't
catch it in the moment.

00:03:32.231 --> 00:03:34.433
Usually comes afterwards,
usually if you're meeting

00:03:34.433 --> 00:03:36.338
with somebody and you do the same thing

00:03:36.338 --> 00:03:38.899
that you always do and you
don't catch it in the moment,

00:03:38.899 --> 00:03:40.593
you catch it the next day.

00:03:40.593 --> 00:03:42.927
Ah, I did it again, I
should have said that,

00:03:42.927 --> 00:03:45.110
I should have done that and
I didn't, I did it again.

00:03:45.110 --> 00:03:47.979
I succumbed to my fear again

00:03:47.979 --> 00:03:50.517
and when you have that
awareness what you'll find is

00:03:50.517 --> 00:03:52.909
the awareness is getting
closer and closer and closer

00:03:52.909 --> 00:03:55.664
and closer to the moment
where it's actually happened.

00:03:55.664 --> 00:03:58.400
So you started off and it's the
next day when you realize it

00:03:58.400 --> 00:04:00.554
and then next time, maybe
a couple of hours later,

00:04:00.554 --> 00:04:01.877
next time's a couple minutes later

00:04:01.877 --> 00:04:03.886
and then you get to that magical moment,

00:04:03.886 --> 00:04:06.717
that magical moment
where you caught yourself

00:04:06.717 --> 00:04:09.122
just before you take the action.

00:04:09.122 --> 00:04:10.763
You're meeting with somebody
and they're giving you

00:04:10.763 --> 00:04:13.696
a project and you're bound to back away,

00:04:13.696 --> 00:04:15.954
the words are about to
come out of your mouth,

00:04:15.954 --> 00:04:18.938
it's about to happen
again, the same pattern

00:04:18.938 --> 00:04:20.875
that you've always done forever and ever

00:04:20.875 --> 00:04:23.628
it's about to come out again
and you had that magical moment

00:04:23.628 --> 00:04:26.878
to catch yourself and choose to be bold

00:04:28.645 --> 00:04:31.025
to overcome the fear to push through it

00:04:31.025 --> 00:04:32.337
and take a separate action.

00:04:32.337 --> 00:04:34.860
Instead of going the
same path you always go,

00:04:34.860 --> 00:04:36.178
swerve and go this way.

00:04:36.178 --> 00:04:38.903
And when you do that,
it gives you the muscle

00:04:38.903 --> 00:04:40.452
to do it again.

00:04:40.452 --> 00:04:41.782
And every time you get to that point,

00:04:41.782 --> 00:04:43.605
it's going to become easier
and easier and easier

00:04:43.605 --> 00:04:44.824
and easier and easier.

00:04:44.824 --> 00:04:47.912
So one for me is understand
what your real fear is,

00:04:47.912 --> 00:04:49.136
know that we have the awareness.

00:04:49.136 --> 00:04:51.544
Two, have a strong enough
why to get out of it.

00:04:51.544 --> 00:04:54.028
And then three, get closer
and closer and closer

00:04:54.028 --> 00:04:55.888
to the moment to where it's happening

00:04:55.888 --> 00:05:00.101
and then choose to be bold,
choose to be powerful,

00:05:00.101 --> 00:05:02.976
and choose to push through your fear.

00:05:02.976 --> 00:05:04.578
So the question of the day is, I'm curious

00:05:04.578 --> 00:05:09.200
what is one of your biggest
fears as it relates to life

00:05:09.200 --> 00:05:11.092
or business, not like a fear of snakes

00:05:11.092 --> 00:05:13.117
but a biggest fear that
you have that you feel

00:05:13.117 --> 00:05:15.469
is holding you back in
your business somehow,

00:05:15.469 --> 00:05:17.611
leave down in the comments,
I'm curious to find out.

00:05:17.611 --> 00:05:19.482
I also want to give a quick
shout out to Paul Rogers.

00:05:19.482 --> 00:05:21.636
Paul thank you so much for
picking up a copy of my book,

00:05:21.636 --> 00:05:24.457
Your One Word, really really
means a lot to me man,

00:05:24.457 --> 00:05:26.465
and I hope you enjoyed the read.

00:05:26.465 --> 00:05:28.099
So thank you guys again for watching,

00:05:28.099 --> 00:05:30.257
I believe in you, I hope
you continue to believe

00:05:30.257 --> 00:05:33.345
in yourself and whatever your one word is.

00:05:33.345 --> 00:05:35.570
Much love and I'll see
you again tomorrow morning

00:05:35.570 --> 00:05:38.397
for another shot of Entspresso.

00:05:38.397 --> 00:05:40.817
♫ I wake up every morning

00:05:40.817 --> 00:05:44.234
♫ Espresso keep me going

00:05:46.727 --> 00:05:50.012
- With every milestone,
while you might be excited

00:05:50.012 --> 00:05:53.066
about the milestone, there's
a part of the milestone

00:05:53.066 --> 00:05:55.777
that you don't want to
face, are you hearing me?

00:05:55.777 --> 00:05:57.947
And listen to me, I've
knocked out the coursework,

00:05:57.947 --> 00:06:00.193
boom, got it done, in order.

00:06:00.193 --> 00:06:03.289
ET, why did it take you two years, ET,

00:06:03.289 --> 00:06:05.261
after you finished your coursework

00:06:05.261 --> 00:06:08.403
why did it take you two
years to get started

00:06:08.403 --> 00:06:09.434
with your dissertation?

00:06:09.434 --> 00:06:13.395
I'm going to be 100 with you,
look knocked all the coursework

00:06:13.395 --> 00:06:16.311
out, but when I finally
got to the dissertation,

00:06:16.311 --> 00:06:17.399
I had to get to that demon.

00:06:17.399 --> 00:06:20.697
I had to deal with, I had
to face it, face what?

00:06:20.697 --> 00:06:23.240
We're not talking about
elementary school, middle school,

00:06:23.240 --> 00:06:27.407
high school, I've had a professor
or two tell me in college

00:06:29.277 --> 00:06:31.261
that you will never get your dissertation,

00:06:31.261 --> 00:06:34.344
that while your writing has improved

00:06:34.344 --> 00:06:37.879
but in terms of your analysis,
like you are not critical

00:06:37.879 --> 00:06:39.361
enough to do a dissertation.

00:06:39.361 --> 00:06:41.239
Are you hearing what I'm telling you?

00:06:41.239 --> 00:06:44.212
We're talking about, man I
love math coming up, why?

00:06:44.212 --> 00:06:48.132
It is what it is, please
excuse my dear aunt Sally.

00:06:48.132 --> 00:06:49.716
Like it is what it is right?

00:06:49.716 --> 00:06:52.694
It's not subjective,
writing is subjective.

00:06:52.694 --> 00:06:54.378
I've had teachers look at my work

00:06:54.378 --> 00:06:58.329
and strip it into parts,
the fear, the fear of what,

00:06:58.329 --> 00:07:00.450
the fear of rejection, right?

00:07:00.450 --> 00:07:02.987
My teachers were so subjective,
I put my whole heart

00:07:02.987 --> 00:07:04.666
into it, I put everything I could put

00:07:04.666 --> 00:07:08.676
and they tell me, edit it
again, revision after revision.

00:07:08.676 --> 00:07:11.777
Edit after edit, are you
hearing what I'm telling you?

00:07:11.777 --> 00:07:13.999
I had to deal with the fact that writing

00:07:13.999 --> 00:07:16.633
had never really been my strong suit

00:07:16.633 --> 00:07:19.867
and even though I worked hard
and put in hours and hours

00:07:19.867 --> 00:07:23.198
in the back mind, in the back of mind,

00:07:23.198 --> 00:07:25.821
I could hear the teachers
say, ET you don't have

00:07:25.821 --> 00:07:27.783
what it takes to get a dissertation.

00:07:27.783 --> 00:07:30.274
I'm a grown man dealing with that fear.

00:07:30.274 --> 00:07:32.330
I'm a grown man dealing with the rejection

00:07:32.330 --> 00:07:36.835
of getting all that red on
my paper of having to do it

00:07:36.835 --> 00:07:39.214
over and over and over and over

00:07:39.214 --> 00:07:41.477
and come on, come on somebody feels me.

00:07:41.477 --> 00:07:44.526
You'll feel like you'll do 120 percent,

00:07:44.526 --> 00:07:47.074
you'll give everything you
have and it still won't

00:07:47.074 --> 00:07:49.859
be enough, I feel you, I was there.

00:07:49.859 --> 00:07:53.068
A part of the milestone is,
what if I give everything

00:07:53.068 --> 00:07:55.561
and it ain't enough, what
if I put my whole heart,

00:07:55.561 --> 00:07:58.306
my whole mind, my whole soul into it ET

00:07:58.306 --> 00:08:01.787
and it's not enough, what
if I do it and I fail?

00:08:01.787 --> 00:08:03.379
So I feel you, so you're just like you not

00:08:03.379 --> 00:08:05.563
going to do it at all because
you'd rather not do it

00:08:05.563 --> 00:08:07.453
and find out the truth and I'm telling you

00:08:07.453 --> 00:08:09.882
you got to do me a favor,
you got to face your fear,

00:08:09.882 --> 00:08:11.094
you got to do it anyway.

00:08:11.094 --> 00:08:14.629
Your boy ET had to face
his fear, that's right,

00:08:14.629 --> 00:08:17.269
I know you see ET, beast
mode, and you're right,

00:08:17.269 --> 00:08:19.504
I am beast mode but it
don't mean beast mode

00:08:19.504 --> 00:08:21.467
without fear, it don't mean beast mode

00:08:21.467 --> 00:08:22.692
without a little anxiety.

00:08:22.692 --> 00:08:25.956
It don't mean beast mode and
I'm just a 120 percent sure.

00:08:25.956 --> 00:08:29.520
No, I have to live by faith
too and I made up in my mind,

00:08:29.520 --> 00:08:31.667
ET, you got to go after it E.

00:08:31.667 --> 00:08:34.425
Look I finished my coursework,
it took me two years, why?

00:08:34.425 --> 00:08:36.961
'Cause it took me two
years to get over the fear.

00:08:36.961 --> 00:08:39.458
It took me two years to
get over the anxiety.

00:08:39.458 --> 00:08:42.419
It took me two years
to finally say, Goliath

00:08:42.419 --> 00:08:45.257
here I come, Goliath, you
might be taller than me,

00:08:45.257 --> 00:08:47.704
you might be bigger than me,
you might be stronger than me,

00:08:47.704 --> 00:08:51.113
but I'm coming and I'd rather die trying.

00:08:51.113 --> 00:08:54.284
I'd rather die going
after this dissertation.

00:08:54.284 --> 00:08:56.026
I'd rather give everything I got,

00:08:56.026 --> 00:09:00.193
I'd rather give a year, I'd
rather put in work and fail,

00:09:01.819 --> 00:09:02.874
then not try at all.

00:09:02.874 --> 00:09:05.574
- There's a scene in there
where you talked about

00:09:05.574 --> 00:09:09.571
bullies and running from
danger and things like that

00:09:09.571 --> 00:09:11.069
when you were trying to help this kid.

00:09:11.069 --> 00:09:13.298
- Yeah, what happens is
this boy is being harassed

00:09:13.298 --> 00:09:16.187
by the neighborhood bully
and his father's encouraging

00:09:16.187 --> 00:09:18.939
his son to beat up this little boy.

00:09:18.939 --> 00:09:21.326
And I wrote this scene, I
wrote this particular scene

00:09:21.326 --> 00:09:23.281
in the script and I was trying to think,

00:09:23.281 --> 00:09:26.202
what can I write to encourage this boy

00:09:26.202 --> 00:09:28.710
to handle the situation,
you know with this bully

00:09:28.710 --> 00:09:30.235
in the neighborhood?

00:09:30.235 --> 00:09:32.441
And I'm spending days
trying to figure out,

00:09:32.441 --> 00:09:34.834
what can I say to boy?

00:09:34.834 --> 00:09:36.720
And finally I came up with the answer

00:09:36.720 --> 00:09:40.256
and it was a situation that
I as a child had encountered

00:09:40.256 --> 00:09:42.862
about his age, I went
to a school in Arizona

00:09:42.862 --> 00:09:45.961
that was mostly Indians
from the reservation.

00:09:45.961 --> 00:09:48.268
And there's this one Indian
kid who just didn't like me

00:09:48.268 --> 00:09:50.702
and every day he chased
me home from school.

00:09:50.702 --> 00:09:54.451
And I had to run by this gas station

00:09:54.451 --> 00:09:56.269
and this mechanic watched me being chased

00:09:56.269 --> 00:09:59.442
by this Indian kid every
day and finally he just

00:09:59.442 --> 00:10:01.447
couldn't handle it
anymore and he stopped me

00:10:01.447 --> 00:10:03.698
and made me face this boy.

00:10:03.698 --> 00:10:07.993
And I told him, I said,
you know I'm scared.

00:10:07.993 --> 00:10:10.002
And he said well, and what he said to me,

00:10:10.002 --> 00:10:13.021
which is still true which
I remember is that he says

00:10:13.021 --> 00:10:17.094
that running from your fear is
more painful than facing it.

00:10:17.094 --> 00:10:18.606
And that's something
I've always remembered.

00:10:18.606 --> 00:10:20.479
And this is what I relate to this boy.

00:10:20.479 --> 00:10:22.629
And of course, eventually
he has to face this fear

00:10:22.629 --> 00:10:23.712
in the film.

